(
        '20519',
        'issues on Screening',
        'Dear Mr. Mohammad,    we have these inquiries to be answered:    Please find attached important issues related to screening  1-We receive two scenarios in screening 888888 and 777777, what is the difference between them?  2-The case management screening appeared in maker accounts only (not seen in checker)?  3-When we upload more than 6000 record for manual field in the list which represent AML -CFT office watchlists, and it appeared only 16 records  4-In watchlist entry for automatically updated lists there are two dates upload date and update date… they are different is that ok?   5-In addition, 27 Nov the screening alerts are about 30000 which is lead us to think there are mistake in the setting ( not like other previous days (every day 20 or less screening alert',
        'Dear @Yad Emdad Karim,    Regarding the points you shared below, please find our responses:    1. Scenarios (888888, 777777):    • Scenario 888888 (Black-list names): usually indicates the standard offline screening process (with black list), where the system performs a full match check against the sanctions and watchlist data based on the provided customer or transaction information.    • Scenario 777777 (Non-BlackList Names) : on the other hand, typically represents a secondary or supplemental check generated by the offline screening engine, often used for refined, rule-based validation or additional list matching logic.    In summary, both scenarios are part of the offline screening alerts, but each one represents a different layer of matching logic, which is why you see two separate scenario IDs.    2. Case Management Screening Appearing Only for Maker Accounts (Not for Checker): This behavior is expected based on the role permissions within the system:    • The Maker role is responsible for initiating, reviewing, and preparing screening cases. Because of that, the system displays all newly generated screening alerts/cases directly in the Maker’s queue.    • The Checker role, however, only sees the cases after the Maker submits them for approval. If the Maker has not yet assigned, completed, or submitted the case, it will not appear under the Checker’s view.    The screening cases appear under the Maker only because they are still in the initial processing stage. Once the Maker completes the required actions and submits the case, it will then become visible to the Checker for review and approval.    3. Uploading More Than 6000 Records for Manual Field (AML-CFT Office Watchlists) but Only 16 Records Appeared: We have checked the list you provided and re-uploaded it without issues. All records loaded correctly as per the provided template. The discrepancy may have occurred due to incomplete or mismatched data in the initial upload. If this issue occurs again, please inform us immediately so we can investigate further.    Note: The list has been uploaded and the names now correctly appeared in the system without any issue.          4. Difference Between “Upload Date” and “Update Date” in Automatically Updated Watchlists: Yes, it is completely normal for the Upload Date and Update Date to be different. Each field reflects a different part of the automatic list-update process:    • Upload Date: This is the date when the list was initially uploaded into the system (the first time it was added). This date does not change unless the list is manually re-uploaded.    • Update Date: This represents the date when the system automatically refreshed or synchronized the list based on the scheduled update job. Since the lists are updated daily (or based on your schedule), this date will continuously change as new data is fetched.    The Upload Date shows when the list first entered the system, while the Update Date shows the most recent automatic refresh.    5. High Number of Screening Alerts on 27 Nov: The high number of alerts on 27 November was caused by duplicate rows generated inside the screening alerts, which resulted in an unusually large count. We have already monitored the data for the affected dates and confirmed the alerts. Additionally, the alerts for 30 November have been resolved, and we will continue monitoring the remaining dates. Any new cases will be handled as soon as possible.    Kindly feel free to reach out if you have any questions or need further clarification.',
        '2025-11-30T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
        '2025-11-30T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
