        'Dear Piotech Team,  I would like to follow up regarding some issues in the name screening process that were previously reported but have not yet been resolved:  •When opening the information page for an entered person, the system first displays an intermediate page before the General Information page. This page allows editing and adding names and numbers, even though it should not appear at all.  •In several attached cases, the General Information page shows details belonging to a different individual rather than the selected person.  •Some generated matching names are not related to the client’s name  •Some of the matches results in a blank page with no information.   •The remaining pending Level 1 alerts from October, listed in the attached Excel file, show blank page when accessing the screening results. No matching names or details appear. We kindly request your support in resolving this issue so that we can complete the pending alerts.  Kindly note that all examples are included in the attachments.  Please let us know if you need any further details.  Thank you',
        'Dears,    I hope this email finds you well.    Based on our web session, please find below PIO-TECH’s responses for each point provided from your end:    • When opening the information page for an entered person, the system first displays an intermediate page before the General Information page. This page allows editing and adding names and numbers, even though it should not appear at all.    ? PIO-TECH Response: After our investigation, we confirmed this is a bug from our side. We have forwarded this case to our development team for review and analysis to ensure it is included in the upcoming release.    • In several attached cases, the General Information page shows details belonging to a different individual rather than the selected person.  • Some generated matching names are not related to the client’s name    ? PIO-TECH Response: The issue has been resolved after checking the AKA tab, which showed that the AKA last name matched the customer’s alert in the provided work case “850831”.           • Some of the matches results in a blank page with no information.     ? PIO-TECH Response: The issue has been resolved by checking the SDNTYPE field in the “General Information” tab and modifying it from “N/A” to “Individual” in the same work case, “850831”.    • The remaining pending Level 1 alerts from October, listed in the attached Excel file, show blank page when accessing the screening results. No matching names or details appear. We kindly request your support in resolving this issue so that we can complete the pending alerts.    ? PIO-TECH Response: After our investigation, we confirmed that the screening results had issues on “07, 24, 25, 26, 27, and 28-Oct-2025” which occurred before the latest fix installation. The issue is now resolved, and the screening results appear correctly for all alerts. Please check and share your feedback.    Please check the responses for the points provided and confirm so we can proceed with closing the ticket below.     Feel free to reach out if you have any questions or need further clarification.    Regards,',
