        '20752',
        'Workflow issue',
        'Workflow issue',
        'Dear Mr. @Mohammad Ammoura,    Based on today’s web session, please find below a status summary of the discussed points, as referenced during yesterday’s meeting with the PIV site:    • Closed Alerts Status:    ? We confirmed that the total number of closed alerts is approximately 27,000 alerts. These alerts were recently closed by our team based on a request from the Bank’s Compliance Department.    ? All related alerts have been closed on 17-Dec-2025, which means they were closed after the investigation conducted on 18-Nov-2025.    • Investigation on 18-Nov-2025:    ? The number of closed alerts reported during the investigation conducted on 18-Nov-2025 was confirmed to be accurate. For your reference, please refer to the file named “AML Alerts for 2025.”    ? The compliance team is able to view closed alerts using the “Compliance” user. Accordingly, the username and password have been shared previously with Bisan via WhatsApp on the same date.      • Review of Bank-Provided Alert Sample:    ? Following our investigation, we confirmed that most of the sampled alerts has been closed under the ticket number “20685” handled by my colleague Ruba. The remaining Approximately 81 alerts remain open with a “New” status. These have been separated in the bank-provided file “Book1” on a sheet titled “Alerts with ‘New’ status” and we have confirmed that they haven’t yet been reviewed or make any action of them.    • Audit Login Trail:    ? The requested “Audit Login Trail” log related to system access monitoring has been provided to Abdulrahman from the bank side after confirming that it is working correctly.    • System Enhancements:    ? To ensure that new and closed alerts don’t disappear for any users, a workaround was implemented on the site by adding an update statement to the dedicated procedure responsible for displaying new and closed alerts, whereby the “Locked By” feature was disabled for these alerts’ status.    ? We confirmed that only one screen for alert display is active on the site. The “Suspected Customer” screen is enabled, while the Case Management screen is disabled, ensuring that both screens don’t operate on the same time and maintaining data integrity at the database level.',
