        '20894',
        'ETL issue',
        'Dears    Kindly note that we ran the provided procedure related to statistics on Friday. However, today the job is throwing the same error as shown below.    We need your urgent support to resolve this issue.    Thank you in advance.',
        'Dear Ahmad,    Based on our web session and the trace analysis of the reported issue, kindly note that the displayed message is a SAP Data Services performance warning, not an error:  “DATAFLOW: Cache statistics for data flow <DF_Branches> are not available to be used for optimization. You must collect statistics before optimization can be done.”    SAP Data Services includes a self-tuning feature in the Execution Properties dialog box called “Collect statistics for optimization.” This feature uses job statistics to determine the optimal cache type (In-memory or Pageable).    In your case, the statistics options were unchecked in the dialog. Kindly ensure that these options are enabled the next time the ETL job is executed. For reference, I have attached a screenshot below showing the required statistics settings. Consider that the ETL daily job for today’s data extraction was completed successfully, as shown below.           Additionally, kindly provide the time at which the DBA runs the daily database backup and the approximate duration required to complete it.    Best Regards,',
