        'Dear Layth     Kindly find below MDSAP replay    “Dear Raed,    This is the SAP standard behavior.    SAP trust only WAF load balancer as source IP, it doesn''t care from which IP or client machine the requests are coming to WAF.  The WAF controls and allows only the permitted IPs configured.    For SAP, always the whitelisted IP or IP''s ranges allowed in WAF load balancer can connect to SAP.    To know all the incoming traffic from external, WAF logs will be the right data. Please review and let me know if you are looking for any specific data from here.    Also, if you want to forward all the incoming traffic IPs to SAP then F5 WAF team has to allow X-Forwarded-For to BOBJ IP. But this is not recommended.      Regards  Ramesha  ”',
